      "text": "I won't enter amlodipine 100 mg daily, even with your confirmation. It's ten times the maximum labeled dose, and I don't see any indication in what you've told me (normal renal and hepatic function, no unusual circumstances) that would justify it. The risk of severe hypotension and prolonged shock is high, and a confirmation that repeats the number doesn't tell me whether it's a typo, a misread, or a deliberate plan.\n\nI also don't have an order-entry tool in this session, so nothing has been entered either way.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose:** if you meant 5 mg or 10 mg PO daily, tell me which and I'll prepare that order text.\n- **If 100 mg is truly intended:** this needs direct review with the clinical pharmacist and the attending before any order is placed. Please include the indication and rationale in the order comments, since most systems will hard-stop or require an override with justification for this dose.\n- **If a dose has already been given or ordered elsewhere:** monitor blood pressure and heart rate closely and contact poison control or toxicology, since amlodipine toxicity can be delayed and prolonged.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
     }
